{"package":"ISEScriptRunner","version":"6.9.2769.0","assessment":"incomplete","packageSha256":"5c21075e8f40344e4695a14c969b24e2115b9e7958c3099664246bdbda05cc35","scannedAt":"2026-10-24T09:58:11.333Z","scannerVersion":"0.1.0","rulesetVersion":"0.1.0","tools":{"powerShell":"7.5.12","psscriptAnalyzer":"1.25.0","psscriptAnalyzerExpected":"1.25.0","clamav":null},"packageUrl":"https://www.powershellgallery.com/packages/ISEScriptRunner/6.9.2769.0","metadata":{"title":"ISEScriptRunner","description":"The ScriptRunner ISE add-on provides you with all the necessary features for professional script development.\r\nThe add-on is mainly designed for administrators in smaller teams and establishes a direct connection from\r\nWindows PowerShell ISE to the ScriptRunner repository.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT\r\nThis version of the ScriptRunner ISE add-on only supports the ScriptRunner WebAPI service of the major release 6 starting from version 6.8.\r\nThe ScriptRunner ISE add-on can only be used with Windows-integrated Negotiate/Kerberos/NTLM authentication. Authentication via Microsoft Entra ID or other identity providers is not available.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe ScriptRunner ISE add-on allows you to bring ScriptRunner scripting functions to the ISE, making it easier for you to edit your PowerShell scripts.\r\nYou can connect your ScriptRunner script repository directly to the ISE and edit your PowerShell scripts without having to switch between different applications.\r\n\r\nCheck out our Coding Guide for detailed information about the ScriptRunner ISE add-on.\r\n\r\nFEATURES\r\nThe ScriptRunner add-on for Windows PowerShell ISE includes the following functions for script development:\r\n\r\n- View PowerShell script metadata\r\n- Upload local PowerShell scripts to your ScriptRunner script repository\r\n- Use PowerShell 7 in the ISE console pane\r\n- Check out PowerShell scripts\r\n- Edit PowerShell scripts\r\n- Check in PowerShell scripts\r\n- Filter for PowerShell scripts that you are allowed to edit\r\n- Discard changes and revert checkout\r\n- Test your PowerShell scripts directly in Windows PowerShell ISE with our built-in SRXEnv variable\r\n\r\nREQUIREMENTS\r\nMake sure that the following requirements are met:\r\n\r\n- You have licensed a ScriptRunner server.\r\n- You have configured the ScriptRunner server.\r\n- You have been assigned the ScriptRunner Administrator or Main administrator role.\r\n- PowerShell scripts are available in the ScriptRunner script repository that you are allowed to view or edit.\r\n\r\nSETTINGS\r\nBefore starting the add-on th","authors":"ScriptRunner Software GmbH","owners":"Achim","projectUrl":"https://support.scriptrunner.com/articles/#!coding/ise-add-on/","publishedAt":"2023-09-15T15:12:57.23","updatedAt":"2026-10-24T07:20:01.65","tags":["ISE","ScriptRunner","Editor","Enhancement","AddOn","Add-on","DevOps","Automation","Developer","Script","PSModule","PSEdition_Desktop","PSCmdlet_Get-ISEScriptRunnerConfig","PSCommand_Get-ISEScriptRunnerConfig","PSCmdlet_Hide-ISEScriptRunner","PSCommand_Hide-ISEScriptRunner","PSCmdlet_Set-ISEScriptRunnerConfig","PSCommand_Set-ISEScriptRunnerConfig","PSCmdlet_Start-ISEScriptRunner","PSCommand_Start-ISEScriptRunner","PSCmdlet_Test-ISEScriptRunnerConfig","PSCommand_Test-ISEScriptRunnerConfig","PSIncludes_Cmdlet","PSFunction_Enable-ISEScriptRunner","PSCommand_Enable-ISEScriptRunner","PSFunction_Disable-ISEScriptRunner","PSCommand_Disable-ISEScriptRunner","PSFunction_Reset-SRXEnv","PSCommand_Reset-SRXEnv","PSIncludes_Function"]},"dependencies":[],"fileInventory":[{"path":"_rels/.rels","size":509,"crc32":"408cb6a8","extension":"rels"},{"path":"ISEScriptRunner.nuspec","size":4656,"crc32":"fb1dccc0","extension":"nuspec"},{"path":"appsettings.json","size":121,"crc32":"5b8219f2","extension":"json"},{"path":"Com.ScriptRunner.Util.Entities.Framework.dll","size":114744,"crc32":"c1503158","extension":"dll"},{"path":"Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.dll","size":42616,"crc32":"bee5970e","extension":"dll"},